The tam_v2 model is a fine-tuned version of Tesseract's Tamil model "tam" from
https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/tessdata_best, licensed under the Apache License 2.0. The
tam_v3 model is a fine-tuned version of tam_v2. The tam_v3.1 models (tam_best_v3.1,
tam_v3.1 and tam_fast_v3.1) are fine-tuned versions of tam_v3.

Training text and ground truth
- Proofread page text from Tamil Wikisource (https://ta.wikisource.org), by the Tamil
  Wikisource contributors, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). The release files
  tam_v2-training-text.txt.gz, tam_v2-wordlist.txt.gz, tam_v2-real-lines.jsonl.gz,
  tam_v3-training-text.txt.gz, tam_v3-wordlist.txt.gz and tam_v3-real-lines.jsonl.gz contain
  this text and are shared under the same licence. Page links are in examples/wikisource-pages.json,
  books/books.json and the line lists.
- Sentences from Tamil Wikipedia (https://ta.wikipedia.org), by the Tamil Wikipedia
  contributors, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0, part of tam_v3-training-text.txt.gz.
- tam.training_text from https://github.com/tesseract-ocr/langdata_lstm (Apache License 2.0),
  part of tam_v2-training-text.txt.gz and tam_v3-training-text.txt.gz.
- The word dictionaries inside the tam_v3 and tam_v3.1 model files contain words from the Tamil
  Wikisource text above.
- English words used to render tam_v3.1 training lines come from SCOWL, Copyright 2000-2011 by
  Kevin Atkinson (Debian package wamerican); the word list is not redistributed.

Scanned page images
- Training lines were cut from page images held by the Internet Archive (https://archive.org),
  mostly copies of the Tamil Virtual Academy / Tamil Digital Library and the Digital Library of
  India, and (for tam_v3) from the Tamil Wikisource scans hosted by Wikimedia. Test pages are
  Tamil Wikisource scans hosted by Wikimedia Commons. The images are not redistributed here;
  the line lists say where each one can be downloaded.

Fonts
- tam_v2 and tam_v3: text lines were rendered with the same 233 font styles. Their sources and
  licences are listed in examples/fonts-v2-open.md, models/tam_v2/fonts.json and
  models/tam_v3/fonts.json.
- tam_multifont (V1, research model, also fine-tuned from "tam"): 188 font styles, listed in
  models/tam_multifont/fonts.json. They include Latha (Microsoft, proprietary) and uniAmma-10,
  -11 and -16 (origin unknown), which have no open licence.
- tam_v2_research (V2-research, research model, also fine-tuned from "tam"): 276 font styles,
  listed in models/tam_v2_research/fonts.json. Besides Latha and uniAmma, they include 45 styles
  of the C-DAC GIST fonts ("Copyright (c) 2005, C-DAC, GIST PUNE, INDIA. FOR NON-COMMERCIAL FREE
  USAGE. For commercial license contact C-DAC, GIST, Pune."). The tam_v2_research model files
  are therefore licensed CC BY-NC 4.0, for non-commercial use only
  (models/tam_v2_research/LICENSE.md), not Apache-2.0.
- tam_v3.1: new text lines were rendered with 23 font files under OFL-1.1 (Noto Sans Tamil,
  Noto Serif Tamil, Mukta Malar, Lohit Tamil, and Noto Sans / Noto Serif for Latin) or
  GPL-3.0-or-later with the font exception (Samyak Tamil), listed in models/tam_v3.1/fonts.tsv.
  A licence review made for tam_v3.1 found that some licences recorded for the tam_v2 / tam_v3
  font styles are unverified or differ from the records; see models/tam_v3.1/LICENSING.md.
- The fonts themselves are not redistributed.

Benchmarks
- RANLP 2025 synthetic Tamil OCR (https://huggingface.co/datasets/Nevidu/tamil_synthetic_ocr)
  and the Tamil OCR Benchmark (https://huggingface.co/datasets/mvbalaji/tamil-ocr-benchmark)
  were used for testing only. Only their scores, and line-group labels computed here, are
  included.
